deep copy
>>> lst1=[1, 2, 3]
>>> lst2=lst1
>>> print(lst1,id(lst1))
[1, 2, 3] 2903699291264
>>> print(lst2,id(lst2))
[1, 2, 3] 2903699291264
>>> lst1 is lst2
True

shalow copy
>>> lst1=[1, 2, 3]
>>> lst2=lst1.copy()
>>> print(lst1,id(lst1))
[1, 2, 3] 2903699442112
>>> print(lst2,id(lst2))
[1, 2, 3] 2903699440320

NOTE: for all the deep copy object is operator returns true.

None data type
--------------------------------
>>> a=None
>>> b=None
>>> print(a,type(a),id(a))
None <class 'NoneType'> 140734987553600
>>> print(b,type(b),id(b))                        ( None is havinge same adress becoz its a keyword )
None <class 'NoneType'> 140734987553600
>>> a is b
True
>>> a is not b
